proposed_comments.body:
These assertions compare the view model with the same mutable settings object, so they cannot detect an accidental change to compatibility defaults. Assert the intended persisted defaults explicitly.

```suggestion
Assert.IsFalse(viewModel.EnableAudibleFeedback);
Assert.IsTrue(viewModel.EnableOpeningSound);
Assert.IsTrue(viewModel.EnableClosingSound);
```

The propagation test assigns the opening-sound setting to its existing default, so it does not prove that the change is sent through the settings callback. Drive both child settings away from their defaults and expect callbacks for the parent plus both children.

```suggestion
viewModel.EnableOpeningSound = false;
...
Assert.AreEqual(3, sendCallbackMock.TimesSent);
...
Assert.IsFalse(mockSettings.Properties.EnableOpeningSound);
```
